# Code-is Basic — slice 3 lowerLocalCodes fixture
library "Code Is Basic".

// A single multi-layer library exercising `code is` local-source lowering end
// to end. Two `code is`-only concepts (lowered to a synthetic local codesystem
// + per-concept code in the Concepts layer, and a `[Resource: <code>]` retrieve
// in the Asserted layer) plus a `defined as` concept composing over them (the
// Inferred layer). The auto-split fans the lowered output across all three
// layers and re-qualifies the cross-layer refs. Because the synthetic
// terminology and its concept land in SEPARATE libraries here (Concepts vs
// Asserted), detectCollisions sees no same-library collision, so NO ` Code`
// suffix fires — the layered code names are bare "<X>" (the ` Code` suffix is
// a per-CRL-only artifact, where terminology + concept co-reside):
//   - the Asserted retrieves' code refs -> "Code Is Basic Concepts"."<X>"
//   - the Inferred composition's concept refs → "Code Is Basic Asserted"."<X>"

// ============ Locally-coded leaves (`code is`) ============

// A PURE QUESTION: a local `code is` boolean with NO derivation and no source representation, so nothing
// can compute it and it is UNKNOWN until a human answers it. It lowers to an "<X> Records" retrieve plus a
// three-state determination (`.answeredValue()` — true / false / null), and the null is what makes a guard
// over it PAUSE and ask rather than deny.
concept "Adult Patient":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- shape is Scalar.
- code is `adult-18-or-older`.

// NOT a question: `exists this` is a derivation over the concept's OWN records, so absence is closed-world
// FALSE and it never pauses. `type is Condition` + `value type is boolean` + `exists this` is the canonical
// spelling — the value type names the RESULT of the `exists`, and this is never re-spelled as an Observation.
concept "Active Crohns Disease":
- type is Condition.
- value type is boolean.
- shape is Scalar.
- code is `active-crohns-disease`.
- definition is exists this.

// ============ Inferred (defined as over the coded leaves) ============

// TWO SEPARATE BOOLEAN FACTS, so this is boolean `and` — not `sem-and`. The bright line: `sem-*` composes
// RECORDS across one concept's representations; `and`/`or`/`not` compose BOOLEANS. Composition is strong
// Kleene, so an unanswered "Adult Patient" makes this null (pause) rather than false (deny) — totality
// belongs at the branch guard, never per operand.
//
// No `type is`: a purely derived composition is EPHEMERAL — it is CQL only and writes no resource, so it has
// no natural resource to name and gets no case-feature StructureDefinition.
concept "Adult With Crohns":
- value type is boolean.
- shape is Scalar.
- defined as
(
   "Adult Patient"
   and
   "Active Crohns Disease"
).
